Package: readaloud
Version: 1.8.14
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Zackarious <https://github.com/Zackarious/ReadAloud>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-glib-2.0, espeak-ng, lame, libportaudio2
Recommends: gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly
Description: Elegant, private, offline Text-to-Speech reader
 ReadAloud is a modern, privacy-respecting Text-to-Speech desktop application
 designed for Linux (GNOME, KDE Plasma, and more) and Windows.
 .
 Features:
  - 100% offline neural voice synthesis with Piper TTS.
  - Pre-bundled natural sounding voice models.
  - Intelligent sentence segmentation and PDF line-break smoothing.
  - Real-time synchronized word highlighting.
  - Wikipedia article importer with live autocomplete.
  - Multi-format audio export (MP3, WAV, OGG, FLAC).
